```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "container_cpu_saturated",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) t, metric, attr_k8s_pod_name pod, round(avg(value),4) v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='container.cpu.usage' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Geo pod container CPU usage rises from about 0.003 cores in the normal period to about 1.6 cores from 12:36 onward."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_deployment_name dep, round(avg(value),3) v FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='container.cpu.time' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT metric, attr_k8s_deployment_name, round(avg(value),3) FROM normal_metrics_sum WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='container.cpu.time' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Geo cumulative container CPU time averages about 207 s in the abnormal period versus about 3.5 s in the normal period."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'a' p, metric, round(avg(value)/1e6,2) mb FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='container.memory.working_set' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'n', metric, round(avg(value)/1e6,2) FROM normal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='container.memory.working_set' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Geo container memory working set rises from about 18 MB to about 27 MB alongside the CPU jump."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'a' p, metric, attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*) c, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'n', metric, attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*), max(value) FROM normal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name='geo' AND metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Geo restart count is 3 in both periods, so the CPU saturation did not come from a new restart or pod."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "geo",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'a' p, span_name, service_name, count(*) c, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'n', span_name, service_name, count(*), round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) FROM normal_traces WHERE span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "search's client span to geo has p95 0.53 ms in both periods; the call path geo to search shows no latency change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'a' p, span_name, service_name, count(*) c, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'n', span_name, service_name, count(*), round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) FROM normal_traces WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Search's Nearby server span p95 is about 10 ms in both periods, with the frontend's Search/Nearby client span unchanged."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The only real anomaly is geo's container CPU saturation, but I could not measure any user-visible effect from it. The fault is confirmed by the metrics. The propagation edges are the call path, not a measured impact.

- **Abnormal vs normal:** The traces are nearly identical in both periods. Latency, error share and span counts are flat for frontend, search, geo, rate, reservation and profile. Logs show no new errors.
- **Geo:** Pod and container CPU rose from about 0.003 to about 1.6 cores starting around 12:36, and its memory working set grew about 50%. Restarts stayed at 3 in both periods and pod uptime did not reset, so this is not a restart or pod failure.
- **Geo's effect on users:** Search's client span to geo and search's own server span are unchanged (p95 about 0.5 ms and 10 ms). Frontend's `/hotels` p95 stayed near 18.7 ms through the whole window. I found no request-level impact.
- **Profile:** Its memcached span moved from 0.29 to 0.31 ms average, which is noise. The one `mongo_profile` span is too little to matter.
- **Not named:** I considered `container_cpu_saturated` versus `process_cpu_saturated`. I chose container-level because pod and container CPU track each other and memory rose too. I did not name any network, HTTP, DB or DNS fault, because the data showed none.

